<title>FRANCE: French election - latest results at 1815 GMT.</title>
<headline>French election - latest results at 1815 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the latest state of the count in the decisive second round of France's election for the 577-seat National Assembly, held on Sunday, according to the Interior Ministry. A total of 289 seats is required for an absolute majority.</p>
<p>The table gives the number of votes won and the percentage share of the national popular vote.</p>
<p> VOTES			   votes won	percentage</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme-left			  0		    0</p>
<p> Communist party		   82,172		9.82</p>
<p> Socialist party		  237,572	     28.41</p>
<p> PRS*				   3,072		0.36</p>
<p> Other left			  41,226		4.93</p>
<p> Ecologists			    0		    0</p>
<p> Independents			  0		    0</p>
<p> RPR**				214,109	     25.60</p>
<p> UDF***			     168,776	     20.18</p>
<p> Other right			 43,144		5.15</p>
<p> National Front		    46,065		5.50</p>
<p> Extreme-right			 0		    0</p>
<p>Total electorate: 1,268,543 Turnout: 65.91 percent</p>
<p>*   Radical Socialist Party (centre-left)</p>
<p>**  Rally for the Republic (Gaullists, ruling coalition)</p>
<p>*** Union for French Democracy (centre-right, ruling coalition)</p>
</text>
